# Waitlist signup endpoint.
#
# The form at site/src/components/WaitlistForm.jsx renders in `npm run dev` regardless, but a
# production build shows the GitHub fallback until this is set.
#
# It must accept a JSON POST of {"email": "someone@example.com"} from the browser and answer with
# CORS headers for the site's origin.
#
# SECURITY: everything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the public JS bundle. This must be a public,
# unauthenticated form endpoint. Never put an API key here — it would ship to every visitor.
#
# The page makes two promises that narrow the choice (see the FAQ and the success panel):
#   1. a confirmation email  — so the provider must support double opt-in
#   2. "one message when Amigo opens" — so it must be able to broadcast to the list later
#
# Providers that can keep both promises:
#   Buttondown     https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/<username>
#   Kit/ConvertKit https://app.kit.com/forms/<form-id>/subscriptions
#   EmailOctopus   embedded form endpoint from their dashboard
#   Loops          https://app.loops.so/api/newsletter-form/<form-id>
#
# Form backends such as Formspark and Formspree are NOT suitable here: they forward a submission
# to your inbox but cannot send a confirmation email or broadcast to the list later, so the copy
# on the page would be untrue.
#
# Turn double opt-in ON in the provider's settings. It is off by default in several of them.
VITE_WAITLIST_ENDPOINT=

# Only needed if your provider does not call the field "email". Buttondown's API wants
# "email_address"; Kit, Loops and EmailOctopus take "email".
VITE_WAITLIST_FIELD=email
